{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"eb481eda734d27c02aaf659e22dbcce1ed1805999ac925e5e055456271ae297d","slug":"clustering-viz","location":"/visual/clustering-viz.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Piece 08 · Clustering visualization, basic to advanced","description":"One neighbourhood dataset, visualised from a raw KMeans scatter up to PCA/t-SNE/UMAP projections, silhouette diagnostics and a seaborn clustermap — with the R pheatmap equivalent at the end.","numbering":{"title":{"offset":1}},"thumbnail":"/clu-main-panel-a350f95f08d2109116d787fd0ed63f84.jpg","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"clustering-viz.md","url":"/clustering-viz-b45751f58ad18665684fc7681190d159.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Clustering visualization","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"key":"rt88XiF7iE"}],"identifier":"clustering-visualization","label":"Clustering visualization","html_id":"clustering-visualization","implicit":true,"key":"y5TwNZiShl"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/clu-main-panel-a350f95f08d2109116d787fd0ed63f84.jpg","alt":"PCA projection, silhouette plot and choose-k curve in one panel","width":"100%","key":"HSZvgNmKRx","urlSource":"figures/clu-main-panel.jpg"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":12,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The finished panel: the three figures that turn “I ran KMeans” into “the clusters\nare real and there are four of them” — a PCA projection (a), a per-sample silhouette\nplot (b), and the silhouette-vs-k curve that justifies k = 4 (c).","position":{"start":{"line":12,"column":1},"end":{"line":12,"column":1}},"key":"SKzjshY9n7"}],"key":"rZp73ubK0B"}],"key":"NXEhQd3Mpu"}],"enumerator":"1","key":"LGVtbw5tFP"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"1 · Why this matters","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"hi0ygl3lZL"}],"identifier":"id-1-why-this-matters","label":"1 · Why this matters","html_id":"id-1-why-this-matters","implicit":true,"key":"tTfnsvYgdZ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Clustering is unsupervised, so the visualization ","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"bgwnTLiinP"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"is","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"u9iJiO23aY"}],"key":"kZfv8dcGxe"},{"type":"text","value":" the result — there is no\naccuracy score to fall back on. This piece walks one dataset from the most naive plot\nto the diagnostics a reviewer expects, answering three questions in order: ","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"AZJfKAM6em"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"can I see\nstructure? how many clusters? are they any good?","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"O7Bf3QKc0N"}],"key":"u8P1vQlTmo"}],"key":"q8f2hh2fWO"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The data is a simulated ","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"mcU7tuEopR"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"city-neighbourhood","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"ugug3mlRJJ"}],"key":"qEQqQ8bust"},{"type":"text","value":" table — 600 neighbourhoods, eight\nsocio-environmental indicators (NDVI, building density, income, PM2.5…), built around\nfour archetypes (green suburb, dense core, industrial, old residential). One dataset\ncarries the whole tutorial:","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"Dn1Oqg7BnD"}],"key":"dds24S6fxe"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","value":"Xs = StandardScaler().fit_transform(df)      # always standardize before distance-based clustering\nkm = KMeans(n_clusters=4, n_init=10, random_state=0).fit(Xs)\nclusters = km.labels_","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"nLelwKZzKJ"},{"type":"admonition","kind":"important","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Important","key":"BwjRlGQ0Fa"}],"key":"ADBnyMfCo4"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Standardize first.","position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"key":"OA5jKqYFxx"}],"key":"y2xjT4YuO3"},{"type":"text","value":" KMeans, PCA, t-SNE and UMAP all use distances; a feature\nmeasured in thousands (land price) would otherwise drown one measured in [0, 1]\n(NDVI). ","position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"key":"YTznWmMhcA"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StandardScaler","position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"key":"q4Yu23957H"},{"type":"text","value":" is not optional.","position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"key":"m3KHfFodT4"}],"key":"DNBeYppZpg"}],"key":"NEPFgSokII"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":41,"column":1},"end":{"line":41,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"2 · Level 1 — the raw scatter","position":{"start":{"line":41,"column":1},"end":{"line":41,"column":1}},"key":"EdS1XbUs9D"}],"identifier":"id-2-level-1-the-raw-scatter","label":"2 · Level 1 — the raw scatter","html_id":"id-2-level-1-the-raw-scatter","implicit":true,"key":"dMCjUB4lDy"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The simplest clustering figure: pick two interpretable features, colour points by\ncluster label, mark the centroids. It is limited (only 2 of 8 dimensions) but it is\nwhere every analysis starts:","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"key":"F9032d9K05"}],"key":"Zvd1RknuPt"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","value":"ax.scatter(df[\"Building density\"], df[\"NDVI\"], c=[PALETTE[i] for i in clusters],\n           s=18, alpha=0.7, edgecolor=\"white\", linewidth=0.3)\n# centroids, mapped back to the original feature units\ncent = StandardScaler().fit(df).inverse_transform(km.cluster_centers_)\nax.scatter(cent[:, b], cent[:, n], c=\"black\", s=180, marker=\"X\", zorder=5)","position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"key":"KyWgKsadpL"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/clu-sub-scatter-b29db7c8957af1742bbc765fb09237e1.jpg","alt":"KMeans clusters on building density vs NDVI with centroids","width":"62%","key":"LPBN3NjLAM","urlSource":"figures/clu-sub-scatter.jpg"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":61,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Green suburbs (high NDVI, low density) separate cleanly here; other pairs of clusters\noverlap — because two features can’t show eight-dimensional separation. That is the\nmotivation for everything below.","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"key":"BAT4pGJ6tB"}],"key":"sLI5xBBmjR"}],"key":"QMoTEN6YOo"}],"enumerator":"2","key":"m9qkESsgH5"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":64,"column":1},"end":{"line":64,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"3 · Level 2 — how many clusters?","position":{"start":{"line":64,"column":1},"end":{"line":64,"column":1}},"key":"noYPUNSLqq"}],"identifier":"id-3-level-2-how-many-clusters","label":"3 · Level 2 — how many clusters?","html_id":"id-3-level-2-how-many-clusters","implicit":true,"key":"iycMhVS582"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":68,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Never trust a ","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"o5RU3h8V3X"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"k","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"T9HS7BPZoC"},{"type":"text","value":" you didn’t test. Two standard curves: the ","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"sCJ553Nb5A"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"elbow","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"asYBhzHVSr"}],"key":"bz4JEckvN2"},{"type":"text","value":" (within-cluster\nSSE, look for the kink) and the ","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"gp0iUziesm"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"silhouette score","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"ibxWbwZtQE"}],"key":"MX8oLPB6uq"},{"type":"text","value":" (look for the peak). Here both\nagree on 4:","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"gBeMreZSvs"}],"key":"uj7Ft2GsBh"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","value":"for k in range(2, 9):\n    m = KMeans(n_clusters=k, n_init=10, random_state=0).fit(Xs)\n    inertias.append(m.inertia_)\n    sils.append(silhouette_score(Xs, m.labels_))","position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":75,"column":1}},"key":"TczPFV5Xlq"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/clu-sub-choosek-93f71b9f70ddc9ecfa5771614d999798.jpg","alt":"Elbow curve and silhouette-score curve, both marking k=4","width":"100%","key":"eB9VP2Uf8j","urlSource":"figures/clu-sub-choosek.jpg"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":82,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The elbow bends and the silhouette peaks at the same k — the reassuring case. When\nthey disagree, prefer the silhouette (it measures separation, not just compactness).","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"key":"KE4nyQ9MuX"}],"key":"r4ZbgQB09t"}],"key":"v0RehKyAP4"}],"enumerator":"3","key":"M2etm3C8Oq"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":85,"column":1},"end":{"line":85,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"4 · Level 3 — PCA, seeing all dimensions at once","position":{"start":{"line":85,"column":1},"end":{"line":85,"column":1}},"key":"ZpwJbB1ULA"}],"identifier":"id-4-level-3-pca-seeing-all-dimensions-at-once","label":"4 · Level 3 — PCA, seeing all dimensions at once","html_id":"id-4-level-3-pca-seeing-all-dimensions-at-once","implicit":true,"key":"Vy6kZdXlMG"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":87,"column":1},"end":{"line":89,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"To see all eight dimensions of separation, project to the directions of greatest\nvariance. Always print the ","position":{"start":{"line":87,"column":1},"end":{"line":87,"column":1}},"key":"jsFc9FoH48"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":87,"column":1},"end":{"line":87,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"explained-variance ratio","position":{"start":{"line":87,"column":1},"end":{"line":87,"column":1}},"key":"C63yJu3RmD"}],"key":"rtaOEaY3Yy"},{"type":"text","value":" on the axes — a projection\nwithout it is unfalsifiable:","position":{"start":{"line":87,"column":1},"end":{"line":87,"column":1}},"key":"oCfEExDGdW"}],"key":"kItnMiwK8O"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","value":"pca = PCA(n_components=3).fit(Xs)\nproj = pca.transform(Xs)\nevr = pca.explained_variance_ratio_ * 100\nax.set_xlabel(f\"PC1 ({evr[0]:.1f}%)\"); ax.set_ylabel(f\"PC2 ({evr[1]:.1f}%)\")","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":96,"column":1}},"key":"RIPg4Xcz2l"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/clu-sub-pca2d-3bb24d10d2bc1acd09cb0230464bdcc6.jpg","alt":"2D PCA projection coloured by cluster","width":"60%","key":"KUVq5MkTVs","urlSource":"figures/clu-sub-pca2d.jpg"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":102,"column":1},"end":{"line":103,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Two components capture ~67% of variance and the four clusters fall apart cleanly —\nthe honest evidence that the structure is real, not a 2-feature artefact.","position":{"start":{"line":102,"column":1},"end":{"line":102,"column":1}},"key":"JWQ4hRpZH3"}],"key":"GD5NoOQac3"}],"key":"jm0GFI70vS"}],"enumerator":"4","key":"h1WneFSkZU"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":106,"column":1},"end":{"line":107,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a third component, matplotlib’s 3D axes add depth (the same viewpoint control as\nPiece 01’s ggcube):","position":{"start":{"line":106,"column":1},"end":{"line":106,"column":1}},"key":"ArjViVJq3T"}],"key":"nWtblqsWP9"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","value":"ax = fig.add_subplot(111, projection=\"3d\")\nax.scatter(proj[:, 0], proj[:, 1], proj[:, 2], c=colors, s=16)\nax.view_init(elev=18, azim=-60)","position":{"start":{"line":109,"column":1},"end":{"line":113,"column":1}},"key":"aljQN5t6zP"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/clu-sub-pca3d-2f0ad1df7a486c531456e19de5bb9102.jpg","alt":"3D PCA scatter of the first three components","width":"60%","key":"BNRTWRG6RQ","urlSource":"figures/clu-sub-pca3d.jpg"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":119,"column":1},"end":{"line":120,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"PC3 adds the separation the 2D view flattens — useful for exploration, though for a\npaper a well-chosen 2D projection usually communicates better (occlusion is real in 3D).","position":{"start":{"line":119,"column":1},"end":{"line":119,"column":1}},"key":"s0pQ74wQis"}],"key":"kB4v78lYiP"}],"key":"f9tDNUhRNt"}],"enumerator":"5","key":"rNK5ZkS0Dh"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":123,"column":1},"end":{"line":123,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"5 · Level 4 — nonlinear projections: t-SNE vs UMAP","position":{"start":{"line":123,"column":1},"end":{"line":123,"column":1}},"key":"ZLiHM5CmBD"}],"identifier":"id-5-level-4-nonlinear-projections-t-sne-vs-umap","label":"5 · Level 4 — nonlinear projections: t-SNE vs UMAP","html_id":"id-5-level-4-nonlinear-projections-t-sne-vs-umap","implicit":true,"key":"IICeqaR8k0"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":125,"column":1},"end":{"line":127,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"PCA is linear; manifold methods bend space to preserve ","position":{"start":{"line":125,"column":1},"end":{"line":125,"column":1}},"key":"pVt47GMfuJ"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":125,"column":1},"end":{"line":125,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"local","position":{"start":{"line":125,"column":1},"end":{"line":125,"column":1}},"key":"bxHF9bbsVt"}],"key":"ZfvGIFDrv3"},{"type":"text","value":" neighbourhoods, often\nseparating clusters PCA leaves touching. t-SNE and UMAP are the two standards — worth\nshowing side by side because they trade off differently:","position":{"start":{"line":125,"column":1},"end":{"line":125,"column":1}},"key":"TySb0zIEBs"}],"key":"WNdVGyPgPM"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","value":"ts = TSNE(n_components=2, perplexity=30, init=\"pca\").fit_transform(Xs)\num = umap.UMAP(n_neighbors=15, min_dist=0.1).fit_transform(Xs)","position":{"start":{"line":129,"column":1},"end":{"line":132,"column":1}},"key":"cZeXw9cOGR"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/clu-sub-manifold-d328a5fdb89565cc6db1c2475615a2de.jpg","alt":"t-SNE and UMAP projections side by side","width":"100%","key":"jhlXd9oTdB","urlSource":"figures/clu-sub-manifold.jpg"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":138,"column":1},"end":{"line":140,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both isolate the four clusters as islands. Caveat for captions: ","position":{"start":{"line":138,"column":1},"end":{"line":138,"column":1}},"key":"GfU1Xfr7aL"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":138,"column":1},"end":{"line":138,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"distances between\nt-SNE/UMAP clusters are not meaningful","position":{"start":{"line":138,"column":1},"end":{"line":138,"column":1}},"key":"sj3BKilGed"}],"key":"C3efhi2c7i"},{"type":"text","value":" — only the grouping is. UMAP better preserves\nglobal layout and is far faster on large data; t-SNE remains the familiar default.","position":{"start":{"line":138,"column":1},"end":{"line":138,"column":1}},"key":"oszy01eG52"}],"key":"LlE2iVKJPo"}],"key":"es0BzMmk0F"}],"enumerator":"6","key":"hJs6p01EWa"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":143,"column":1},"end":{"line":143,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"6 · Level 5 — silhouette diagnostics","position":{"start":{"line":143,"column":1},"end":{"line":143,"column":1}},"key":"WlmRZFsbdS"}],"identifier":"id-6-level-5-silhouette-diagnostics","label":"6 · Level 5 — silhouette diagnostics","html_id":"id-6-level-5-silhouette-diagnostics","implicit":true,"key":"rzomgJhb0L"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":145,"column":1},"end":{"line":147,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The number ","position":{"start":{"line":145,"column":1},"end":{"line":145,"column":1}},"key":"rzuwbUWo7j"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"silhouette_score = 0.53","position":{"start":{"line":145,"column":1},"end":{"line":145,"column":1}},"key":"ltNEAxmcAX"},{"type":"text","value":" hides the distribution. The per-sample\nsilhouette “knife” plot shows every point’s fit: wide blades = tight clusters,\nnegative values = misassigned points:","position":{"start":{"line":145,"column":1},"end":{"line":145,"column":1}},"key":"rCMCS9JEcf"}],"key":"rDZaK4QARg"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","value":"sil_vals = silhouette_samples(Xs, clusters)\nfor i in range(K):\n    vals = np.sort(sil_vals[clusters == i])\n    ax.fill_betweenx(np.arange(lo, lo + len(vals)), 0, vals, facecolor=PALETTE[i])\nax.axvline(silhouette_score(Xs, clusters), color=\"#EE6C4D\", ls=\"--\")","position":{"start":{"line":149,"column":1},"end":{"line":155,"column":1}},"key":"SR93KZAXp1"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/clu-sub-silhouette-0d36eb36816d7272998251e20d5598cc.jpg","alt":"Per-sample silhouette knife plot for the four clusters","width":"60%","key":"umvw4sih4l","urlSource":"figures/clu-sub-silhouette.jpg"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":161,"column":1},"end":{"line":162,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Four blades, all mostly right of the mean line, few negatives — the visual proof that\nk = 4 produced clean clusters, not just a good average number.","position":{"start":{"line":161,"column":1},"end":{"line":161,"column":1}},"key":"a7SXeEDC3P"}],"key":"qJgb3wnfNh"}],"key":"Zvu7RUmUKC"}],"enumerator":"7","key":"X6CpCputV5"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":165,"column":1},"end":{"line":165,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"7 · Level 6 — the clustermap (a heatmap with dendrograms)","p